.claude/skills/playwright-cli/
# Installed agent-skill content (Remotion + remotion-bits). Reproduce it with
# `npx skills install` — skills-lock.json pins every source + hash and IS tracked.
# The .claude/skills/* entries are absolute symlinks into this checkout, so they are
# machine-specific and must never be committed.
/.agents/skills/*
# Project-owned daily production skill; keep other installed skills local.
!/.agents/skills/mental-empire-daily-production/
!/.agents/skills/mental-empire-daily-production/**
/.claude/skills/*
.playwright-cli/
.playwright-mcp/
.playwright/
.junie/

# Local scratch / diagnostic dumps (API body captures, temp probes)
scratchpad/
scratchpad-bodies/
tmp/
tmp-*/
/resources/video-engine/remotion-bundle/

# Local user-data snapshot used by scripts/seed-restore.* — may contain the
# user's real sources/channels/library, so the data files stay local-only.
# The scripts and docs under scripts/ and seed/ ARE tracked.
/seed/snapshot/*.db
/seed/snapshot/*.db-wal
/seed/snapshot/*.db-shm
/seed/snapshot/*.json
# Data-level channel + API-key seed written by scripts/seed-channels.cjs. Holds the
# real channel inventory and the API keys in PLAINTEXT — never commit it.
/seed/channels-seed.json

# Ad-hoc Playwright a11y snapshot dumps saved at repo root during exploration.
# (electron-builder.yml is tracked packaging config — do not blanket-ignore *.yml)
/login.yaml
/after-login.yaml
/create-page.yaml
/pre-delete.yml
/tv-*.yaml
/tv-*.yml
scratch/
changes.diff
# Claude Code session-recovery runtime state
HANDOFF.md
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/rate-limit-state.json
.claude/stop-failure-events.jsonl
.claude/quota-blocked.json

# Kilo machine-local preferences. Shared project config under .kilo/ — commands in
# .kilo/command/*.md and agents in .kilo/agent/*.md — stays tracked; this file only carries
# per-machine editor settings such as `snapshot`, so committing it churns the tree across
# checkouts without configuring anything the project depends on.
.kilo/kilo.jsonc

# Benchmark media is regenerated on demand from BENCH_BROLL_SPECS in
# scripts/bench-render-assets.ts via `npm run bench:render`. ~70 MB of synthetic 1080p, plus
# the cached `ungraded-*.mp4` masters `--grade-only` leaves behind, which push the directory
# to several hundred MB. Not worth committing; test/fixtures/bench-render/project.json is.
test/fixtures/bench-render/assets/
# Rewritten on every bench run, so committing it would leave the tree permanently dirty —
# and nothing reads it back, so it locks nothing. Regenerated, not authoritative.
test/fixtures/bench-render/assets.lock.json
.codex/
.kilo/
.superpowers/
.env
.env.*
*.env
credentials.json
*.pem
*.key
.credentials
flowmusic-session/chrome-profile/
